From: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "sched/mmcid: Switch over to the new mechanism"

This reverts commit 653fda7ae73d8033dedb65537acac0c2c287dc3f.

I managed to locally reproduce the issue seen by the CI since v6.19-rc1
using:

  $ cd <kernel source code>
  $ echo 'echo OK' > .virtme-exec-run
  # docker run -v "${PWD}:${PWD}:rw" -w "${PWD}" --rm -it \
      --privileged mptcp/mptcp-upstream-virtme-docker:latest \
      build normal
  # i=1; \
    while docker run -v "${PWD}:${PWD}:rw" -w "${PWD}" --rm \
    -it --privileged mptcp/mptcp-upstream-virtme-docker:latest \
    vm auto normal; do \
      echo "== Attempt: $i: OK =="; \
      i=$((i+1)); \
    done; \
    echo "== Failure after $i attempts =="

'git bisect' between v6.18 and v6.19-rc1 pointed me to this commit.
Reverting it on top of v6.19-rc1 fixes the issue there. Reverting it on
top of Linus' tree caused conflicts, resolved here. (I never touched
kernel/sched/core.c, so hopefully my innocent conflicts resolution was
OK.)

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/b24ffcb3-09d5-4e48-9070-0b69bc654281@kernel.org
Link: https://github.com/multipath-tcp/mptcp_net-next/issues/617
Signed-off-by: Matthieu Baerts (NGI0) <matttbe@kernel.org>
